# Facts of isMutating: what one wire call says (cmd, args), read by the host as typed values. Absence is its own state: args.hasEnable is a bool, the switches are absent|off|on.
# off = the literal false (False or "false"; for fix: any falsy value), on = any other present value. call.base = the registry (read|write|unknown); call.actionRead = the catalog lists args.action as a read of call.cmd.
CONTRACT unitymcp.mutability
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE mutability_facts
FACT call.base enum=read,write,unknown closed
FACT call.cmd string
FACT call.unknownIsWrite bool
FACT call.actionRead bool
FACT args.action string
FACT args.hasEnable bool
FACT args.fix enum=absent,off,on closed
FACT args.reset enum=absent,off,on closed
FACT args.abortOnFail enum=absent,off,on closed
FACT args.clear enum=absent,off,on closed
INPUT isMutating call.base call.cmd call.unknownIsWrite call.actionRead args.action args.hasEnable args.fix args.reset args.abortOnFail args.clear
